.TH PSModelSetName 3 2023-12-03 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSModelSetName

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/psyc.h>

.I
int  
.br
\fBPSModelSetName\fR(\fIPSModel *model\fR, \fIchar *name\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the name of \fImodel\fR with the string provided with the argument \fIname\fR.
.br
If \fIname\fR is \fINULL\fR and \fImodel\fR already has a name, model's \fIname\fR will be cleared.
.br

.br
\fBNOTE\fR:  the model will duplicate the provided \fIname\fR and it will keep it inside its internal data. The duplicated string will be automatically freed by freeing the whole model (\fIPSModelFree\fR). If \fImodel\fR already has a name, the original name will be automatically freed.
.br

.SH RETURN VALUES
1 is name is successfully set or 0 if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fImodel\fR is \fINULL\fR.
.br

\[bu] memory cannot be allocated.
.br
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
PSModelFree(3)
